<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Region Worksheet ~ the practice, held as a spine

''Spine law:'' the source MD chapters stay canonical until this spine renders the practice
whole — `sdm/…/Synthetic_Dream_Machine_06_Campaign_Regions.md` (the Region chassis, the
OGA-mode table craft, and the SDM Campaign Region Worksheet proper) and the FTLS-04 Area
profile. Verbatim text lands in #source as fenced MD blocks; uplift to live wikitext runs
last, after every slot reads as moved.

''The fractal worksheet law'' (stated once, here — the nexus worksheets enact it, never
re-state it): a Realm-hex worksheet holds the 30-mile view; each named Destination earns a
Travel-hex place meme on its shelf; Sites and Areas that matter (extraction, delving, RSS
profiles) nest beneath their Destinations. Every place meme declares its stratum and its
hex-scale. Feed every hex: ''horizon · hidden handle · bleed''.

Live enactments: [[new-delos|../../../../@elyncia/ha.ka.ba/elyncia/nexuses/new-delos/region-worksheet.md]] ·
[[illyria|../../../../@elyncia/ha.ka.ba/elyncia/nexuses/illyria/region-worksheet.md]] ·
neo-thracia (referee bag).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-scale-ladder>>

!! The Scale Ladder //(Provisional — pace claim flagged below)//

Nested 1:6:5:5, bound to canon time units:

| Hex | Span | Pace | Runs on |
|---|---|---|---|
| ''Site'' | 1 mile | delve & search | 10-minute Turns |
| ''Travel'' | 6 miles | the horizon; 1 hex ≈ 1 watch off-route | watches (4 h — FTLS `04:143`) |
| ''Realm'' | 30 miles | one road-day for a caravan; factions, armies, rumors | days -> the week cadence |
| ''Reach'' | 150 miles | biomes, plates, empires | seasons |

The Realm hex names the worksheet's home scale (the "nexus-scale subhex" of the gradient
canon). ''Pace flag:'' the 6-mile/watch off-route rate
contradicts nothing on disk — SDM/UVG travel runs week-scale with no sub-week mileage stated
— but the external UVG book stays unchecked; the rate fills a gap, so it firms only through
table play.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-three-map-kinds>>

!! Three Map-Kinds

* ''Places'' — Destinations, Discoveries, Areas, and their RSS Nodes (the RSS senses kept;
  nothing renamed under them).
* ''Routes'' — the pointcrawl legs (roads, rivers, ley-lines, void-lanes). On-route travel
  runs the destination procedure at week scale, no hex navigation — the UVG system stated
  plainly.
* ''Ambient'' — the field between (SDM-06's own word: the world's breathing): the Area's
  Tags + Arcane + Tech, read off the Realm worksheet. Off-route, the Ambient activates.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-travel-loop>>

!! The Travel Loop ~ on-route and off

''On-route:'' skip straight to the destination procedure (week scale, supplies, misfortune,
encounters, arrival — Quickstart `01:1723`).

''Off-route, the Ambient activates'' — watch-scale crawl: declare direction and method ->
spend one watch and resources -> navigate (a miss drifts the party one hex and clouds the
map) -> read the hex's horizon line; working the hex opens the hidden handle -> encounter
check per the FTLS-04 Encounter Roll under its ''Attention'' bands (never a flat 1-in-6),
content drawn from the bleed line or the pre-rolled stack.

''The hex-entry law:'' every operational Travel hex carries three worksheet lines, never
fewer — ''1. the horizon'' (what entering eyes see) · ''2. the hidden handle'' (found only
by working the hex; often an RSS Node) · ''3. the bleed'' (one active vector leaking into
neighbors; feeds the encounter stack and the ambient tables).

<<~/ahu>>

